WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.650
For applications, risk sets the chain.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:07.850
Every app gets a risk tier from the identity
governance officer before anyone gets

3
00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:11.316
access, and one high-risk trait
is enough to make it Tier 1:

4
00:00:11.316 --> 00:00:15.988
an application permission, sensitive
data, an outside operator, or no owner.

5
00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:18.689
The tier then decides who approves access,

6
00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:21.775
who approves consent, and
how often it's reviewed.

7
00:00:21.775 --> 00:00:24.528
Consent is the riskiest
request you'll see,

8
00:00:24.528 --> 00:00:28.775
because a grant covers the whole
tenant at once and never expires.

9
00:00:28.775 --> 00:00:31.802
So any application permission
gets Tier 1 handling,

10
00:00:31.802 --> 00:00:36.025
and critical scopes need the governance
officer and the CISO together.

11
00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:39.619
The decision: tier every
app before the first grant,

12
00:00:39.619 --> 00:00:43.213
and treat anything untiered
or ownerless as Tier 1.

13
00:00:43.213 --> 00:00:45.460
Next, apps as identities.
